      "description": "Watch Twente vs PSV Eindhoven highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 20, 2026. The Eredivisie delivered a high-stakes encounter on Sunday, September 20, 2026 , as two of the league's heavyweights locked horns in a clash filled with tactical drama. The atmosphere in the stadium was electric, setting the stage for a game where the momentum would swing violently between both sides. PSV Respond to Early Twente Opener Twente wasted little time in asserting themselves on home turf. In the 14th minute, Younes Taha found the back of the net with a clinical left-footed strike, giving the hosts an early lead. However, the joy was short-lived as PSV Eindhoven began to dominate possession, controlling 60% of the ball. The visitors' pressure told quickly through the clinical finishing of Guus Til . In the 26th minute, Guus Til rose highest to head home an equalizer from a Mauro Junior cross. Just three minutes later, PSV turned the game on its head. A brilliant team move involving a key pass from Ruben van Bommel and an assist by Paul Wanner allowed Guus Til to slot home his second with a right-footed finish. The first half ended with rising tempers, as Wout Weghorst received a yellow card for dissent as the teams headed for the break with PSV leading 2-1. Late Drama Seals a Famous Victory The second half saw a more physical battle, with both Ruben van Bommel and Ivan Perisic entering the referee's book. Twente struggled to break down the PSV defense for long periods, but the introduction of fresh legs like Daan Rots proved decisive. In the 79th minute, Wout Weghorst made amends for his earlier booking by smashing home the equalizer following an assist from Rots . With the momentum firmly behind them, Twente pushed for a winner. It arrived in the 83rd minute when Daouda Weidmann connected with a Max Bruns pass to fire home with his right foot. Despite late pressure from the visitors and several corners, the Twente defense held firm. In front of a crowd of 30,000, the final whistle confirmed a remarkable 3-2 victory for Twente , who managed to carve out a win despite PSV ’s territorial dominance throughout the match."
